em that is baked into the code at the point of ingestion.\n\nI concede that strict liability has a role in addressing catastrophic, singular events like a model hallucinating incorrect medical advice or triggering a critical infrastructure failure. However, my argument depends on the assumption that the most significant societal damage is not a single, explosive event, but the slow, systemic degradation of user autonomy through ubiquitous, non-defective data extraction. If this assumption is wrong and the primary threat is indeed a discrete, catastrophic failure rather than systemic erosion, then the focus on data minimization would be insufficient. Nevertheless, until we address the incentive to extract, we are merely taxing the shovel while the machine continues to mine our consciousness.",
